Terraform AWS IAM Role Configuration
This task involved automating the creation of an AWS IAM role using Terraform with a variable-driven configuration name.

Task Overview
Environment: IAC Server / VS Code Workspace (/home/bob/terraform)

Objective: Create an AWS IAM role named via a Terraform variable.

Requirements:

Store the IAM role name (iamrole_anita) in a variable named KKE_iamrole inside variables.tf.

Structure the Terraform configuration with a main.tf file referencing variables.tf.

Configuration Files
1. variables.tf
Terraform
variable "KKE_iamrole" {
  description = "The name of the AWS IAM role"
  type        = string
  default     = "iamrole_anita"
}
2. main.tf
Terraform
resource "aws_iam_role" "anita_role" {
  name = var.KKE_iamrole

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}
Execution Steps
Initialize Terraform:

Bash
terraform init
Apply Configuration:

Bash
terraform apply -auto-approve
Verification & Results
Apply Output: Apply complete! Resources: 1 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed.

Result: The IAM role iamrole_anita was successfully created and provisioned on AWS through the configured Terraform script.
